{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793845810,"nonce":"wy1CMblHoRSIfXgTTihWAbxnhhA=","title":"Tiered worker saturation spills compilation onto interpreter and extra OSR threads","message":"With dedicated compile workers enabled, tick_callback compiles synchronously when a hot unqueued function arrives while all workers are busy. Interpreted OSR requests spawn another promotion thread in the same situation. This bypasses the configured worker budget and allows whole-entry and region optimization to compete. Keep hot calls interpreted while worker requests wait; prioritize active OSR requests within the existing queue. Preserve synchronous fallback when workers are explicitly disabled or all worker starts fail. Validate saturation, stale-demand retry, shutdown, no-worker fallback, native promotion and complete TypeScript official conformance; measure frozen binaries on the NUC before concluding a performance benefit. Related: 65bf647 (worker overspeculation), 53de327 (method_call), 978ab39 (static-hot policy).","files":null}]}